From 39993aaeee04d9d95c509258f1249318754ff227 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chen Ni <nichen@iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Mon, 23 Sep 2024 10:15:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 389/960] iommu/arm-smmu-v3: Convert comma to semicolon

commit 7de7d35429aa2e9667e51b88ff097be968feaf8f upstream.

Replace comma between expressions with semicolons.

Using a ',' in place of a ';' can have unintended side effects.
Although that is not the case here, it is seems best to use ';'
unless ',' is intended.

Found by inspection.
No functional change intended.
Compile tested only.

Fixes: e3b1be2e73db ("iommu/arm-smmu-v3: Reorganize struct arm_smmu_ctx_desc_cfg")
Signed-off-by: Chen Ni <nichen@iscas.ac.cn>
Reviewed-by: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Lu Baolu <baolu.lu@linux.intel.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20240923021557.3432068-1-nichen@iscas.ac.cn
Signed-off-by: Will Deacon <will@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Kunkun Jiang <jiangkunkun@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Yihua Jin <jinyihua@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Li Wei <liwei818@huawei.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.c
index 7bdb12ed1ec1..a52e47a2d351 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.c
@@ -1377,7 +1377,7 @@ static int arm_smmu_alloc_cd_tables(struct arm_smmu_master *master)
 		cd_table->s1fmt = STRTAB_STE_0_S1FMT_LINEAR;
 		cd_table->linear.num_ents = max_contexts;
 
-		l1size = max_contexts * sizeof(struct arm_smmu_cd),
+		l1size = max_contexts * sizeof(struct arm_smmu_cd);
 		cd_table->linear.table = dma_alloc_coherent(smmu->dev, l1size,
 							    &cd_table->cdtab_dma,
 							    GFP_KERNEL);
-- 
